{
  "context": "fold 0 only, effnetv2s, seed 42, 20 epochs, last-epoch checkpoints. Fold 0 is the label-noisy fold (session-stamped AP-ROP labels): every image-level AP-ROP recall here is depressed by that, which is the evaluation-unit finding, not a model property. Single-fold numbers carry no error bars; only large gaps are interpretable.",
  "readings": [
    "The sampling confound is closed from both sides and changes nothing: flat holds with or without the sampler (QWK 0.603 weighted / 0.580 natural), while the CORN head only trains at natural prevalence (0.129 weighted). The flat-vs-structured CV equivalence stands on either sampling regime.",
    "Four arms are statistically indistinguishable on this fold (flat-natural 0.580, no_branch 0.575, full 0.569, flat-weighted 0.603 QWK) \u2014 single-fold gaps this size are noise, per this project's own rule.",
    "The two decisive gaps: +sampler on CORN collapses to 0.129, and no_ordinal decays to 0.394 \u2014 but no_ordinal held 0.645 at epoch 16 before a 4-epoch slide, and flat softmax at natural prevalence is fine, so read it as training instability of the masked-softmax+branch combination, not proof that softmax cannot rank. Last-epoch discipline reports the decay either way.",
    "The adversary does not help: w0 0.648 vs w0.5 0.569 fold-0 QWK, cross-site tied (0.942 vs 0.946) \u2014 consistent with the disease-controlled probe finding.",
    "Session-level AP-ROP scoring (ablation_session_level.json) lifts EVERY arm \u2014 0.73-0.95 recall with overlapping CIs on 22 sessions, flat-natural highest, and even the sampler-collapsed arm recovers to 0.909. The branch shows no session-level advantage either: its remaining justification is taxonomy fidelity (an independent AP-ROP probability, as ICROP-3 defines the form), not any measured recall gain. The evaluation-unit finding is model-independent, which is exactly what makes it a finding about the labels rather than about any architecture."
  ],
